  "version": "0.34.0",
  "notes": "Palette v0.34.0 brings reviewable folder updates, built-in Palette documentation for your agents, and a handful of reliability fixes.\n\n### New\n\n- **Review folder updates before they land** — when a session picks up changes to your folder, you get to look them over and decide before they're applied.\n- **Palette documentation built in** — agents can now look up Palette's own documentation while they work, without any setup.\n- **Shared HTML files in Organisational context** — HTML documents shared with your organisation now show up alongside the rest of your context.\n- **Automatic runtime updates** — Palette checks its managed tools for updates when you launch the app and when you switch back to it.\n\n### Improved\n\n- **New sessions start faster** — sessions are ready to use sooner, with setup finishing in the background.\n- **Smarter detection of tools already on your Mac** — Palette now only uses a coding tool it finds on your machine if it's a recent enough version to work properly.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **Codex model list stays accurate** — the list of available Codex models is now checked against the version Palette is actually running, so you won't see models that aren't there.\n- **Tool permission prompts match the right request** — permission requests are now correctly paired with the action asking for them.\n- **Working Slack community link** — the invite link in Help now points at a fresh invite that actually works.",
